{
  "verdict": "incorrect",
  "p_correct": 0.03,
  "errors": [
    "The demand constraint requires inflow >= need and ignores each region's own stock. The correct balance is supply + inflow - outflow >= need. Regions with a surplus, such as Region 1 (268 vs 165), should not need to import anything.",
    "Because of this, the model ships out nearly all stock and then re-imports the full need. For example, Region 1 ships out 268 yet receives 165, and Region 5 ships out 465 yet receives 439. This inflates the transport cost, so 17249 is far above the true minimum."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Fractional units allowed (the data are integral, so this is harmless)."
  ],
  "reason": "The model does not let a region use its own supply to cover its need, so it ships far more than necessary and the objective is overstated."
}
